  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="19428a02-c8bd-5ddc-8e00-92552da33e87" activityNameId="06c084b6-7fcd-5b74-a0ca-3d196ca52f03" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Use, computer, desktop with LCD monitor, sleep/standby mode</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Use, computer, desktop with LCD monitor, sleep/standby mode
The computer desktop use in the standby/sleep mode includes the share of computer production (CPU, keyboard, mouse, LCD) as well as the energy consumption (use-phase) and the rail and road transport from factory to user. Energy consumption of computer CPUs and LCD monitors (use-phase) vary a lot depending on the computer looked at. Min.-Max. values are listed;
Synonyms: PC; 
UUID: b1b670bc-473a-3e69-afeb-9464ef91ec58
Describes the use of a desktop computer with a LCD monitor in the standby/sleep mode. Calculated per 1 hour of computer use. Computer life span assumed to be 4 years, for the LCD monitor 6 years. Standby/sleep mode 2 hours a day (office use), 240 days a year. UCTE production mix applied for electricity consumption (low voltage).
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: No technology involved, except for the production of the desktop computer (including LCD, keyboard and mouse), which is described in another dataset.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Manufacturers, literature and own assumptions. 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: International data suitable for Europe.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_b1b670bc-473a-3e69-afeb-9464ef91ec58.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
